      "author": "@Roy-xc1mz",
      "text": "/STUDY COMMANDS\n\n/blueprint       Map the whole topic from foundations to advanced ideas\n/firstprinciples Reduce it to fundamental truths, then rebuild it\n/eli5            Explain it in extremely simple terms\n/explain         Give a clear normal explanation\n/deepdive        Explore the topic in serious detail\n/layers          Explain at beginner → intermediate → expert levels\n\n/mindmap         Organise the topic into a visual hierarchy\n/cheatsheet      Create a compact reference sheet\n/onepage         Fit the essential topic onto one conceptual page\n/summary         Give a concise summary\n/keyideas        Extract only the most important ideas\n/80-20           Teach the small set of ideas that gives most understanding\n/taxonomy        Show categories, subcategories and relationships\n/framework       Build a reusable mental model\n/connections     Connect the topic to related concepts\n/timeline        Explain it chronologically\n/prereqs         Show what I need to understand first\n/roadmap         Give me an ordered learning path\n\n/intuition       Build intuitive understanding\n/technical       Give the precise technical explanation\n/practical       Focus on real-world use\n/how             Explain how it works\n/why             Explain why it happens\n/mechanism       Explain exactly what happens under the hood\n/analogy         Teach through analogies\n/visual          Explain spatially or visually\n/example         Teach through examples\n/case            Teach through a realistic case study\n/walkthrough     Take me through it step by step\n/jargon          Translate specialist language into plain English\n/vocab           Teach the important terminology\n/formulas        Explain the important equations and variables\n\n/flash           Turn the topic into flashcards\n/recall          Test me using active-recall questions\n/quiz            Quiz me and mark my answers\n/exam            Give me harder exam-style questions\n/drill           Repeated practice until I understand it\n/socratic        Teach by questioning me\n/feynman         Make the idea simple enough to teach clearly\n/teachback       Make me explain it, then identify weaknesses\n/diagnose        Find the gaps in my understanding\n/challenge       Challenge my assumptions and understanding\n\n/compare         Compare concepts side by side\n/versus          Focus on differences and trade-offs\n/mistakes        Show common mistakes and traps\n/mythcheck       Separate misconceptions from established facts\n/questions       Show the important questions I should be asking\n/memoryhooks     Create mnemonics and memory aids",
